      "message": "fix(sim): the wire gouge reading says how deep the kerf enters\n\nThe kerf law read the clearance of a move that stands in the product\nas 0, so each such gouge read the kerf offset alone (0.162 mm on a\n2.8 mm entry). The law now reads a signed clearance: minus how far the\nmove's deepest point stands inside the product. The depth is the kerf\nreach plus that distance. The verdict does not change.\n\nFixes #3211\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
